    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"Figure 4. 25 IDM vehicles on a 1 km ring with an extreme \
phantom-jam configuration (v0=30 m/s, T=2.5 s, a=0.3 m/s^2, b=2.0 m/s^2). At \
t=0 the cars are visibly spaced out (40 m mean gap) at free-flow speed. A \
single-vehicle speed perturbation amplifies; by t=400 s the ring has a \
deep-red cluster of near-stopped cars (slowest ~0.8 m/s) next to a green \
free-flow arc (fastest ~17 m/s). Bottom panel: accumulating space-time \
trajectory diagram (time along x, position along y with wrap-around at 1000 \
m). The backward-travelling jam wave is the diagonal red band - cars move \
forward (slope up-right) but the jam drifts backward relative to them. (MP4: \
Wolfram/results/anim_idm.mp4.)\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->520]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{20, 20}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"08d8cacb-3c2d-4560-9049-901bd33fe8ef"],

Cell["5. The simplest car-following that jams: Bando OVM", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"73686d37-0fd2-4684-8466-7134db40f18e"],

Cell["\<\
Even simpler than IDM, the Optimal Velocity Model (Bando et al. 1995) relaxes \
speed towards a target velocity that depends only on the gap to the vehicle \
ahead:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e98462ce-ebda-4d32-869d-013fe767de81"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    SubscriptBox["v", "\[Alpha]"], "\[CenterDot]"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"\[Kappa]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["V", "opt"], "(", 
      SubscriptBox["s", "\[Alpha]"], ")", "-", 
      SubscriptBox["v", "\[Alpha]"]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"d9011356-35a7-43d6-8b4a-a1193ef37e8d"],

Cell["with the standard choice", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"494126b1-f460-44f0-967e-15708716a992"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["V", "opt"], "(", "s", ")"}], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["v", "max"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"tanh", "(", 
       RowBox[{
        FractionBox["s", 
         SubscriptBox["s", "c"]], "-", "2"}], ")"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"tanh", "(", "2", ")"}], ")"}]}], 
    RowBox[{"1", "+", 
     RowBox[{"tanh", "(", "2", ")"}]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",\

 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"eda2971b-b735-4c50-934b-124504722fb4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The model has a single stability parameter, the sensitivity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Kappa]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "c8b1f407-c8d6-4308-b87b-4d755f1dd8dc"],
 ". For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Kappa]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "65812cf2-d621-4506-8433-50e21cdef4cd"],
 " above a critical value the uniform-flow solution is stable; below it, \
uniform flow is linearly unstable via a Hopf bifurcation and the system \
collapses into stop-and-go waves. This is the cleanest mathematical \
explanation for why phantom jams exist: they are the attractor of a dynamical \
bifurcation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"304e2873-16af-4abb-a80c-f588ed9a384b"],

