    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"Figure 5. Bando OVM on an 800 m ring with 18 vehicles and \
kappa=0.4, below the stability threshold 2 V_opt'(s*) ~ 0.61. Top: ring \
snapshot showing the orange-red stop-and-go cluster and green free-flow \
regions. Bottom: accumulating space-time trajectory diagram \[Dash] the \
diagonal orange bands drifting backward relative to the car trajectories are \
the stop-and-go waves. Speed spread grows over time as the Hopf instability \
saturates. (MP4: Wolfram/results/anim_bando.mp4.)\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->520]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{20, 20}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"a2307409-db7f-4c10-bc7a-b9fddd4dbcc5"],

Cell["6. A stochastic cellular automaton: Nagel-Schreckenberg", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5b44607e-739c-4a76-913f-77531631938c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nagel and Schreckenberg (1992) gave the minimal CA that reproduces \
realistic traffic dynamics. Space is discretised into 7.5\[ThinSpace]m cells, \
time into 1\[ThinSpace]s steps, and velocity is an integer in [0, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["v", "max"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "e40dadb5-a8c0-470f-803f-033e61e0cd80"],
 "]. At each step every vehicle applies four rules:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15f74908-af67-4b47-aa99-308484deb35a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "1", ")", " ", 
   RowBox[{"accelerate", ":"}], " ", "v", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"min", "(", 
    RowBox[{"v", "+", "1"}], ",", " ", 
    SubscriptBox["v", "max"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"53679f11-cd67-45a7-b267-bec3434800d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "2", ")", " ", 
   RowBox[{"brake", ":"}], " ", "v", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"min", "(", "v", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"d", "-", "1"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"5adedf3f-6f3e-4356-a5c9-07ca8c25e604"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "3", ")", " ", 
   RowBox[{"randomise", ":"}], " ", 
   RowBox[{"with", " ", "probability", " ", "p"}], ",", " ", "v", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"max", "(", 
    RowBox[{"v", "-", "1"}], ",", " ", "0", ")"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"c42b2feb-1b37-4d87-b0ef-25e21f527996"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"(", "4", ")", " ", 
   RowBox[{"move", ":"}], " ", "x", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"x", "+", "v"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"11ad1977-d86e-4445-8eca-676d10927947"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["d", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "e031755b-7d11-4886-b67d-87c423e923e8"],
 " is the number of empty cells to the next vehicle. The stochastic slow-down \
rule (3) is essential: without it the model reduces to a deterministic CA and \
does not jam spontaneously. With it, the space-time diagram spontaneously \
generates backward-propagating \"wave\" bands, matching the LWR and IDM \
results from a completely different starting point."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9e1ad3b6-f6b3-4dcb-a10d-c3edba2ef0a4"],

